WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.200
- Oh, don't come and sneak up on me!

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.989
Don't sneak up!

00:00:03.989 --> 00:00:06.656
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.310
Hey tasty, it's me, Danny Trejo

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.200
and as you can probably guess

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.560
one of my favorite things
to do is to cook tacos.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.840
Today, I'm going to show you

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.940
three of my favorite recipes.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.440
First up, is a quick and
delicious 10-minute Shrimp Taco.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.060
Next is a savory 1-hour
Fried Chicken Taco.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:32.370
And if you really wanna impress,

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:34.920
I'm going to show you a Brisket Taco

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.110
that takes a full day to make.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:39.303
Now let's get cooking!

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:44.100
Okay first up is our Shrimp Diablo Taco.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.240
Now, the machete is not
needed for this recipe.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:52.530
Start with our roasted
garlic, chipotle sauce,

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:57.123
our olive oil, garlic powder, salt, honey,

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:00.420
like the way I did that, it was cool.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.700
And then our lemon juice.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.096
All these go into the blender
to make our Diablo sauce.

00:01:06.096 --> 00:01:07.710
(blender whirring)

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:10.140
You know I used a blender
in a movie before,

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.093
you make people tell you something.

00:01:12.093 --> 00:01:13.200
Ooh!

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.460
Mix it well.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.020
Now we've got a bowl of shrimp

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.740
mixed very very well with our Diablo sauce

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.330
this is a quick marinade,

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:23.340
and then we're going to grill it.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:24.900
We got our pan nice and hot.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.700
Now an old trick that I learned

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.590
was putting oil on one side

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:29.910
and just doing this,

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.890
that way it's evenly spread.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.270
Oh yeah!

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:34.710
Two to three minutes,

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:35.543
flip it over

00:01:35.543 --> 00:01:37.170
and the nice thing about shrimp

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:41.550
is that it cooks fast and
it's absolutely delicious

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:44.220
especially with the Diablo sauce.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.630
That's the kicker.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:50.040
Okay now these start to
look nice, good and crispy,

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.263
smell absolutely delicious.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.013
Please sir, may I have another?

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:01.230
Okay now, we're almost done
with the Shrimp Diablo.

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:05.250
Get our tortillas that
you've put in the oven

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:08.760
wrapped in tinfoil for about five minutes.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.320
What I always like to do

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.970
is put the guacamole first

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:14.460
so that it'll spread on the tortilla

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:16.410
and then cabbage and pickled onion,

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.510
this is what we're mixing up right now.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:22.260
Next are piece (indistinct) or shrimp,

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.120
never skimp on the shrimp.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.503
Now just a little cilantro,

00:02:25.503 --> 00:02:27.510
some people don't like cilantro.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:31.053
Then of course our lime juice.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.113
Delicious!

00:02:33.113 --> 00:02:36.450
For a 10 minute taco, this can't be beat

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:38.703
and kids don't talk with your mouthful.

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:43.710
(upbeat music)

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:46.350
Up next is our Fried Chicken Taco

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:47.850
now that's a winner.

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:49.860
First step is our flour.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:51.480
Pour our flour in here,

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.140
next garlic powder, onion powder,

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:59.901
oregano, paprika, little bit of cayenne,

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:01.050
of course some salt

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.880
and black pepper.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:07.770
Then what we're doing is
using chicken thighs and mix

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:09.930
little bit with the buttermilk.

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:13.050
Chicken's looking good
and we're ready to move on

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.430
to our next step.

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:17.100
Once it gets to 350 we're ready to go.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.680
From the buttermilk, to the flour,

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.080
make sure you mix it real good

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.970
and then shake it off,

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.203
and then just, whoa!

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:28.290
It's been about seven minutes

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.690
and our chicken is looking good.

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:35.690
You're looking for a real nice
golden brown crispy cover.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:39.000
Okay now we're gonna
make our chipotle cream.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.510
Sour cream, next is our chipotle peppers

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.250
with adobo sauce.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.380
Salt, our lime juice.

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:49.333
It's my favorite part,
operating heavy machinery.

00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:52.020
(blender whirring)

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.540
We're gonna put about a quarter cup

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.550
into our cabbage,

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.100
salt and pepper

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.182
and a little bit of
olive oil, mix this up,

00:04:02.182 --> 00:04:03.330
oh yeah!

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:06.360
And really this is good just like this.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:08.370
Pico de gallo was one
of my favorite sauces.

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:10.380
Our pico de gallo what we've got,

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.750
chips of jalapeno, red onions,

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:17.280
and then the tomato,
cilantro, our lemon juice,

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.370
a little salt, some olive oil.

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:22.680
We wanted to do a healthy taco

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:24.240
with a little bit of protein.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:27.390
So what we did was get lettuce, cabbage,

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:29.103
and then we got our pico de gallo.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.490
Let's do a little more sauce

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:37.490
and here is your perfect
1-hour Fried Chicken Taco.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:42.780
Next is the Barbacoa Brisket Taco.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:46.590
Now this was inspired by my
mom's recipe for Barbacoa.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.060
So the first step, salt,

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.910
next sugar, next is cumin,

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:53.670
pepper and garlic.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:55.590
Now what we do is this,

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:59.340
we're putting this all
over this brisket, okay?

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:01.050
Set this in plastic,

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:04.500
let it sit for approximately eight hours.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:07.980
That's right, you heard it, eight hours.

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:11.700
Now, believe me, this
one's really worth it.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:13.500
Now the key to this recipe

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:14.793
is the three B's,

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:18.990
brine, browning and braise.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.090
Right now we are going to brown.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:23.693
Neutral oil, there it is.

00:05:23.693 --> 00:05:24.526
Ooh!

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:27.090
Oh yeah!

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.530
Sizzle, sizzle, sizzle,

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:30.113
mom, you watching?

00:05:30.113 --> 00:05:31.830
(Danny chuckles)

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:34.020
All right now I'm turning
this over right now.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.940
That's Browning.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:37.740
You don't wanna get it any more than that.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.420
Through the other side,

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:41.940
this is real good and brown

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.700
so here we go, put this over here,

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:46.230
now we get to our sauce.

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:48.840
First, naturally our onion,

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:52.980
garlic, coriander, cumin, chili powder.

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:57.120
We get our vinegar, bay
leaves and tomatoes.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:00.480
And these, we crush up with our hand,

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:01.770
looking good!

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:04.380
Next, we got our chipotle,

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:06.570
this takes a little while sometimes

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:09.180
it is our molasses.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.620
Last but not least

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.300
is a cup and a half of water.

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.610
Now this is packed with flavor.

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:16.800
We're gonna put our brisket in here.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:18.900
Soaking up all 'em juices.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:20.190
We're gonna cover this

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:22.410
and then bring this to a boil.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:25.350
Okay now this is pretty well at a boil

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:27.450
so now what we'll do,

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.730
get this, cover it,

00:06:29.730 --> 00:06:32.100
and we'll put the lid back on.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:36.120
Put the oven at 350,
cook it for eight hours.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:37.560
Just brought this out of the oven,

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:38.640
pulled the brisket out,

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:41.220
we've reduced the broth by half.

00:06:41.220 --> 00:06:44.820
Now, at Trejo's we don't
even touch the brisket

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:47.040
until we can pull it apart

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:48.960
with just two forks like that.

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:50.460
Oh yeah!

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.293
Here we go.

00:06:51.293 --> 00:06:53.040
Oh now!

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.290
Hey the brisket came out great!

00:06:55.290 --> 00:06:56.670
Like always.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:58.950
Remember, first goes the tortillas

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:00.950
and then goes our brisket

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:03.720
oh this smells delicious already.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:05.490
Little bit of pico de gallo,

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:07.650
we've got our Cotija cheese,

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:10.233
and don't forget the tortilla strips.

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.220
There's no words to describe

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:16.890
what's going on in my mouth right now.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.630
All right, there you have it.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:20.250
Three tacos.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.440
You've got Shrimp Diablo,

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:24.480
you've got Fried Chicken

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.790
and you've got the Barbacoa brisket.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:29.040
If you have trouble,
it's all in the cookbook.

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:29.880
All of it.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.650
Hey, thank you for watching,

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:32.580
get cooking

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:35.073
or I hope to see you at the restaurants.

